 /**
+ * timekeeping_skip - advance every clock by @nsecs without the clocksource moving
+ * @nsecs:	nanoseconds of CLOCK_MONOTONIC to skip
+ *
+ * The timekeeper accumulates the skipped interval as if the clocksource
+ * had counted through it: the cycles @nsecs take at the current,
+ * NTP-adjusted rate (rounded up) are added to the cycles since its last
+ * update, and it catches up at once, as after a long idle. So to the whole
+ * system the skip looks like ordinary elapsed time: CLOCK_MONOTONIC moves
+ * by @nsecs, CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW by those cycles at its own rate, and NTP's
+ * frequency, slew and leap seconds apply to the skipped seconds too.
+ * Catching up at once also keeps the vDSO's cycle delta small. Called
+ * with interrupts off.
+ */
+static bool timekeeping_advance(enum timekeeping_adv_mode mode);
